namespace OpenEMR\Services;

final class NoteSearchService extends BaseService
{
    private const MAX_SNIPPET_LENGTH = 200;
    private const MAX_LIMIT = 10;

    public function searchPatientNotes(int $patientId, string $query, int $limit = 5): array
    {
        $limit = min($limit, self::MAX_LIMIT);

        // Single table search with patient scoping first
        $sql = "
            SELECT id, date, title, 
                   MATCH(body) AGAINST (? IN NATURAL LANGUAGE MODE) AS relevance_score,
                   SUBSTRING(body, 1, ?) AS snippet
            FROM pnotes
            WHERE pid = ? 
              AND MATCH(body) AGAINST (? IN NATURAL LANGUAGE MODE)
            ORDER BY relevance_score DESC
            LIMIT ?
        ";

        return QueryUtils::fetchRecords($sql, [
            $query, self::MAX_SNIPPET_LENGTH, $patientId, $query, $limit
        ]);
    }
}
```

Key implementation details:
1. Use prepared statements exclusively - never concatenate user input
2. Patient ID filter in WHERE clause evaluated before FULLTEXT (MySQL optimizer behavior)
3. Return relevance score for result ranking
4. Truncate snippet to 200 chars for response size management

